    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d476">

                <pb facs="0634" n="528" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg528"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister O’Brien to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Copenhagen</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-05-14"><hi rendition="#italic">May 14,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 101.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In dispatch No. 59<anchor n="a"
                        xml:id="d476-f1"/> from this legation, dated December 19 last, reference was
                    made to arbitration treaties between Denmark and Italy.</p>
                <p>Just before the adjournment of the Rigsdag this treaty was ratified, and I
                    venture to inclose herewith a translation.</p>
                <p>The noticeable feature of the convention is found in article 1, by which all
                    differences which they are themselves not able to adjust shall be submitted to
                    the permanent court of arbitration at The Hague.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. T. O’Brien.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d476-a1.xml" xpointer="d476-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
